> It appears that when candles are affixed to the candelabrum, their
> weight diminishes or disappear.

An empty lamp weighs as much as a full one.

A candle, while burning up, keeps weighing the same, until it's burnt up,
when it suddenly loses all its weight at once.

In NetHack, every item has a fixed weight. This includes the Candelabrum.
If attaching the candles would change this weight, you'd have to change
the whole of the item handling, which would in my opinion be a major fuss
for nothing.

Of course, you could also introduce a new object: "the Candelabrum of
Evocation with candles affixed". A good thing that wax candles and tallow
candles weigh the same, or you would have to define eight different
Candelabra. Really, there should be only one!

